**Time & Aspect:** Present · Simple

**Structure:** `subject + base verb (+s/es)`

Habits, routines, permanent facts, timetables, and general truths.

**Signal words:** always, usually, every day, often, never, on Mondays

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"The sun rises in the east."}

- {"l":"–","t":"She does not work on Sundays."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Do they live here?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Present · Continuous

**Structure:** `am / is / are + verb-ing`

Actions happening now, temporary situations, and fixed future arrangements.

**Signal words:** now, at the moment, currently, these days, look!, listen!

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"They are watching a film."}

- {"l":"–","t":"He is not sleeping."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Are you coming tonight?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Present · Perfect

**Structure:** `have / has + past participle`

Past actions with a present result, experiences, and unfinished time periods.

**Signal words:** just, already, yet, ever, never, since, for, recently

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"I have finished my work."}

- {"l":"–","t":"She has not arrived yet."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Have you ever been to Delhi?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Present · Perfect Continuous

**Structure:** `have / has been + verb-ing`

An action that began in the past and is still going on, stressing duration.

**Signal words:** since, for, all day, how long, lately

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"They have been waiting for an hour."}

- {"l":"–","t":"It has not been raining long."}

- {"l":"?","t":"How long have you been learning English?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Past · Simple

**Structure:** `verb + -ed  /  irregular form`

Completed actions at a definite past time, and a sequence of past events.

**Signal words:** yesterday, ago, last week, in 2010, then, when

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"We visited Imphal last year."}

- {"l":"–","t":"He did not call me."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Did she pass the exam?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Past · Continuous

**Structure:** `was / were + verb-ing`

An action in progress at a past moment, often interrupted by a shorter action.

**Signal words:** while, when, as, at 8 pm yesterday, all morning

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"I was reading when she called."}

- {"l":"–","t":"They were not listening."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Were you sleeping at midnight?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Past · Perfect

**Structure:** `had + past participle`

The earlier of two past actions — the 'past before the past'.

**Signal words:** before, after, by the time, already, until then

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"The train had left before we arrived."}

- {"l":"–","t":"She had not eaten anything."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Had they finished by noon?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Past · Perfect Continuous

**Structure:** `had been + verb-ing`

Duration of an action that continued up to a point in the past.

**Signal words:** for, since, before, how long

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"He had been working for hours before he rested."}

- {"l":"–","t":"We had not been waiting long."}

- {"l":"?","t":"How long had she been studying?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Future · Simple

**Structure:** `will + base verb`

Predictions, instant decisions, promises, and offers.

**Signal words:** tomorrow, soon, next week, in the future, probably, I think

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"I will help you."}

- {"l":"–","t":"They will not come."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Will you join us?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Future · Continuous

**Structure:** `will be + verb-ing`

An action that will be in progress at a specific future moment.

**Signal words:** this time tomorrow, at 9 pm tonight, still

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"This time tomorrow I will be flying home."}

- {"l":"–","t":"He will not be working on Sunday."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Will you be using the car?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Future · Perfect

**Structure:** `will have + past participle`

An action that will be completed before a point in the future.

**Signal words:** by, by then, before, by the time, in two years

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"By 2030 I will have graduated."}

- {"l":"–","t":"She will not have finished by five."}

- {"l":"?","t":"Will they have left by noon?"}

**Time & Aspect:** Future · Perfect Continuous

**Structure:** `will have been + verb-ing`

Duration of an action up to a point in the future.

**Signal words:** by, for, by the time, by then

**Examples:**

- {"l":"+","t":"By June I will have been teaching for ten years."}

- {"l":"–","t":"He will not have been living here long."}

- {"l":"?","t":"How long will you have been working?"}
